**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`

**How to implement.** The reviewed experiment's points in the Data step, each with Exclude or Include, and a chart in which an excluded point stays, marked (001 §O 'Data dialog: … per-point exclusion with a reason'; 001 §K 'exclusions carry a reason and stay visible in plots, marked'; the S9.3 brief; .spec-md §4 'UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`, after the inline chart: `PointMark` = `KeptPointMark` | `ExcludedPointMark`; `PlottedPoint = { position : ConstructorUiPosition; point : ChartPoint; mark : PointMark }`; and `pointsChartView (id : ConstructorUiId) (points : PlottedPoint list) (xLabel : ControlCaption) (yLabel : ControlCaption) : IView`, documented in one to three lines: a `Canvas` carrying `id`, of the inline chart's size, drawn with the private `PlotWindow.over`, `gridLines`, `axisLines` and `axisLabels` the bay's chart is drawn with (called, not copied; `PlotWindow.over` takes the points as one series); each kept point a filled 5 × 5 `Ellipse` in the first series colour carrying `dataPointDot position`, and each excluded point an unfilled 9 × 9 `Ellipse` ring with a red stroke of 1.5 carrying `dataExcludedPointMark position`, each centred on its point. No line joins the points. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type MappedPointNumber with member this.uiPosition : ConstructorUiPosition` (its value); `type MappedPoints with member this.pointCaptions : ControlCaption list`, one per point in order, numbers by `%g`: an intensity point `x = <x>, I = <intensity>`, an ellipsometric point `λ = <nm> nm, Ψ = <ψ>°, Δ = <δ>°`, a capture row `<label> #<capture index>: <description>° → <avg_total>`, an observation `<key> <T or R>: θ = <incidence>°, φ = <azimuth>°, m00 = <m00>` and a mapped row `<its scan cells' display values joined by ", ">: <signal, or m00>`; and `member this.chartPoints : ExperimentControls.ChartPoint list`, one per point, x its 1-based number and y its reading's first value (the intensity, Ψ in degrees, `avg_total`, the observation's m00, or the mapped signal or m00). On `ConstructorUiId`: `static member dataReviewButton (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataReview_<id>`), `static member dataPointRow (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataPoint_<n>`), `static member dataExcludePointButton (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataExcludePoint_<n>`) and `static member dataIncludePointButton (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataIncludePoint_<n>`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group, each with a one-line doc: `dataReviewPanel` (`"DataReviewPanel"`), `dataExclusionReasonField` (`"DataExclusionReasonField"`), `dataPointsChart` (`"DataPointsChart"`), `dataPointDot (point : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$"DataPointDot_{point.value}"`) and `dataExcludedPointMark (point : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$"DataPointExcluded_{point.value}"`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: each `dataFileRow` gains, after its attach verb, the verb `Review` carrying `dataReviewButton experiment.id` and sending `ReviewExperimentData experiment.id` (step 315), offered read-only too. When `model.reviewedDataOpt` is `Some r`, after the split panel, a bordered panel carrying `dataReviewPanel`: the heading `Points of <name> — <its badge text>` (`model.dataBadgeOf`, step 295); a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Reason:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `dataExclusionReasonField` that shows `model.dataDraft.exclusionReason` and sends `SetExclusionReason` on Enter and on losing focus; for `r.points = Ok points`, `ExperimentControls.pointsChartView ConstructorUiId.dataPointsChart` of the `chartPoints` marked `ExcludedPointMark` where the experiment's data excludes the point (`tryFindExclusion`, step 313), with the labels `point` and `reading`, and then one row per point carrying `dataPointRow n`: `#<n>  <its caption>` and, for an excluded point, `excluded — <reason>` in the message colour and the verb `Include` (`dataIncludePointButton n`, sending `IncludePoint`), otherwise the verb `Exclude` (`dataExcludePointButton n`, sending `ExcludePoint (id, n, model.dataDraft.exclusionReason)`), both disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`; for `Error e`, `e`'s caption. No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests` (step 324): `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `DataReviewPanel`, `DataExclusionReasonField`, `DataPointsChart`, `DataPointDot_2`, `DataPointExcluded_2`, `DataReview_1`, `DataPoint_2`, `DataExcludePoint_2` and `DataIncludePoint_2`. New `each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number`: the captions and chart points of a two-point intensity series, two Phone ROI rows and one observation (test-local) are as listed above, each x its number. `the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings`: over the class's model whose data proxy is a mock answering E1's attachment with the series `0 → 1.0`, `45 → 0.5`, `90 → 0.0` and whose E1 data excludes point 2 for `beam blocked`, after `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 1)`, the panel shows three point rows, row 2 reading `excluded — beam blocked` with `Include` and rows 1 and 3 `Exclude`, and the chart holds `DataPointDot_1`, `DataPointDot_3` and `DataPointExcluded_2` and no `DataPointDot_2`. `pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back`: over a recording dispatch with the reason field holding `stray light`, pressing `Exclude` of point 3 records `ExcludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 3, ControlCaption "stray light")` and pressing `Include` of point 2 records `IncludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2)`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart`: in the rendered Data step over that model, pressing `dataReviewButton` of E1 shows `dataReviewPanel` and `dataPointsChart`.

**Acceptance.** After the review panel lands, the Data step MUST review an experiment's points with each point's caption, an excluded point listed with its reason and drawn as a ring on the chart beside the kept dots, Exclude sending the typed reason and Include taking an exclusion back, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number`, `the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings` and `pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
